MID_EV11_000_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_000_m01_001: Cai! Over there!
MID_EV11_000_m01_002: Alright, we got you now! Yah! Huh?
MID_EV11_000_m01_003: Great. There it goes, off again. Get it together,\nyou two!
MID_EV11_000_m01_004: Let's hurry after it! We're gonna catch this thing!
MID_EV11_000_m01_005: Ha! We've got it cornered!
MID_EV11_000_m01_007: A pure white ornius is very rare. I've never seen\nanything like this one.
MID_EV11_000_m01_008: H-hey, Cai...are you sure it's OK for us to catch\nthis thing?
MID_EV11_000_m01_009: It's not like a servant to a god or anything, right?\nFortuna's altar is pretty close to here...
MID_EV11_000_m01_010: <NCA>Agree with him.
MID_EV11_000_m01_011: <NCB>Downplay the danger.
MID_EV11_000_m01_027: <ACA>Now that you mention it, this bird does feel different\nfrom the others.
MID_EV11_000_m01_012: <ACA>Yeah... I mean, it's got a strange vibe to it.
MID_EV11_000_m01_013: <ACA>You don't have to agree with him, Cai. Just think\nabout how valuable this ornius is!
MID_EV11_000_m01_028: <ACB>Uh... I'm sure it's fine. Probably. Maybe.
MID_EV11_000_m01_014: <ACB>I don't wanna get some kinda curse by touching it.
MID_EV11_000_m01_015: <ACB>Enough already! Peter, you worry about everything!
MID_EV11_000_m01_016: Oh! Hey! This one's a girl!
MID_EV11_000_m01_017: She can lay big eggs for us in the village. We'll eat\nomelets until we're stuffed!
MID_EV11_000_m01_019: Oooh, I'll ask Mom to cook 'em up for Cai's\nbirthday tomorrow!
MID_EV11_000_m01_020: OK. Gonna give it one more try...
MID_EV11_000_m01_022: Grurururu...
MID_EV11_000_m01_023: Heeey... Are you angry? Don't be angry!
MID_EV11_000_m01_024: Good girl. Stay calm. Please, stay calm.
MID_EV11_000_m01_025: Get ready! Here she comes!
MID_EV11_000_m01_026: Gweeeeeh!
MID_EV11_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_001_m01_040: You are Hell's-Eye Cai, one of the Flame Lords of\nDagda. Am I mistaken?
MID_EV11_001_m01_041: My name is Cai, but... What's going on? What is this?
MID_EV11_001_m01_042: A swirling vortex of causality yawns before you.
MID_EV11_001_m01_043: You will have many difficult trials ahead. Seek me\nout when you have overcome them.
MID_EV11_001_m01_044: Keep this Divine Sand close at hand, and I shall\nnever be far from you.
MID_EV11_001_m01_045: O...K...
MID_EV11_001_m01_055: 
MID_EV11_001_m01_046: <NCA>Say thank you.
MID_EV11_001_m01_047: I don't get it, but...thanks.
MID_EV11_001_m01_048: Hmm...
MID_EV11_001_m01_049: Was...that a dream?
MID_EV11_001_m01_050: Cai!
MID_EV11_001_m01_003: You're saying you met a pure-white being with a bird\non their shoulder...here...at Fortuna's shrine.
MID_EV11_001_m01_005: White being, strange presence, white bird... It's just\nlike the Herald of the Pale Raven!
MID_EV11_001_m01_006: Hey, I know that one! It goes like... Uh... How does\nit go?
MID_EV11_001_m01_007: <NCA>Ask Peter.
MID_EV11_001_m01_008: <NCB>Ask Tialla.
MID_EV11_001_m01_051: <ACA>Tell me, Peter.
MID_EV11_001_m01_009: <ACA>The ruler of heaven changes into two people, and\nreally bad stuff starts happening.
MID_EV11_001_m01_010: <ACA>And then this golden shiny crown flashes real bright,\nand the world explodes, and everybody dies.
MID_EV11_001_m01_011: <ACA>Peter! You're oversimplifying it! Here's how it goes...
MID_EV11_001_m01_052: <ACB>Tell me, Tialla.
MID_EV11_001_m01_012: "When the pole star splits in two, dark power will fill\nthe land, and the world's foundations will shake.
MID_EV11_001_m01_013: "When the zodiac takes the golden crown, a flute will\nsound, telling the world of the twilight of the living."
MID_EV11_001_m01_014: It's a verse from a really old poem left by\nJehoshaphat, a prophet of the Ostoro people.
MID_EV11_001_m01_016: I also heard that the white bird god will send the\nPromised One to rescue the world.
MID_EV11_001_m01_017: Also known as the Herald of the Pale Raven, right?\nYeah, I heard that from a mage in the village.
MID_EV11_001_m01_018: Hmm... What's a "Paul Star"?
MID_EV11_001_m01_019: A POLE STAR, Cai! Like a north star? One of the\nstars in the north sky that's always in the same spot?
MID_EV11_001_m01_022: Huh. There they are—the north stars. So there's a\nbright one and a darker one next to it. Two stars...
MID_EV11_001_m01_023: Wow. It's not even that dark yet, but you can already\nsee the stars?
MID_EV11_001_m01_024: You've got really good eyes, Peter. I'm jealous.
MID_EV11_001_m01_025: But if you think about it, the pole stars have been\ntwo stars for ages.
MID_EV11_001_m01_026: I guess the prophecy is dumb, then. If it was true, the\nworld would have been destroyed by now, right?
MID_EV11_001_m01_027: {SetColor=Gray}Huh? What he said just now... Why did it sound\nso familiar?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_001_m01_028: How did it feel to upheave the world?
MID_EV11_001_m01_029: Cai? Wake up! You're zoning out.
MID_EV11_001_m01_053: Oh. Uh, sorry. I was just thinking about a weird\ndream I had.
MID_EV11_001_m01_054: I was sitting in this big room, and this powerful\nwoman walked down some stairs...
MID_EV11_001_m01_030: And then... Aw, it's no big deal. But, hey, Tialla...\nYou know a lot about the stars, huh?
MID_EV11_001_m01_031: Only because I read...a lot. Grandpa's got a ton of\nbooks at home.
MID_EV11_001_m01_038: Oh! Grandpa! I forgot I have to run an errand\nfor him!
MID_EV11_001_m01_039: I need to go! Cai, Peter—sorry. See you tomorrow!
MID_EV11_069_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_069_m01_001: Hello! Anyone home? Hellooo!
MID_EV11_069_m01_002: Uh... Hello? You're from the temples, right? What's\ngoing on here?
MID_EV11_069_m01_003: Hmm? Do you live here? Oh... You look a lot like\nyour mother.
MID_EV11_069_m01_004: My mom? What do you know about my mom?
MID_EV11_069_m01_005: Oh, uh... Never mind that. Is your father here?
MID_EV11_069_m01_006: Pop's usually out and about at this hour.
MID_EV11_069_m01_007: I guess he'll be back by morning though...probably.
MID_EV11_069_m01_008: If that's the case, I'll ask you to pass along a message.
MID_EV11_069_m01_009: Just tell him "It's tomorrow." Say that to him, and\nwe'll be good.
MID_EV11_069_m01_010: "It's tomorrow"? What's tomorrow? My birthday's\ntomorrow.
MID_EV11_069_m01_011: I know. And I think you've got the message now.
MID_EV11_069_m01_012: Have we...met before?
MID_EV11_069_m01_013: Yeah, but you wouldn't remember much about it.
MID_EV11_069_m01_014: I need to get going. Deliver the message.
MID_EV11_069_m01_015: I'm done with this stupid day.
MID_EV11_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_002_m01_046: 
MID_EV11_002_m01_001: *snore*
MID_EV11_002_m01_002: Mmm...
MID_EV11_002_m01_003: Huh? Ah!
MID_EV11_002_m01_004: Not a chance!
MID_EV11_002_m01_005: Huh?
MID_EV11_002_m01_006: Gah!
MID_EV11_002_m01_007: What?! Again?! I've told you a thousand times—the\nstatue is not a shield!
MID_EV11_002_m01_008: But, I mean, it's the perfect size, perfect weight.
MID_EV11_002_m01_009: Haven't I always said, "Think of the statue as Aurora\nherself"?! Forgive us, Aurora!
MID_EV11_002_m01_010: Why can't you just come into the house like a\nnormal person?
MID_EV11_002_m01_011: Why does it always have to be a home-invasion drill\nwith you, Pop?
MID_EV11_002_m01_012: Can't let your guard down, even when you're asleep.\nThe door opens, you focus.
MID_EV11_002_m01_013: You get raided a lot just minding your own business?\nI don't think so.
MID_EV11_002_m01_014: It's about protecting what's important.\nRemember that.
MID_EV11_002_m01_015: Why do we have a statue of Aurora anyway?\nFortuna's temple's closer to the village.
MID_EV11_002_m01_017: Real smart. It's not about how close the temple is.\nIt's about Aurora's beauty.
MID_EV11_002_m01_018: Pop...have you ever seen Aurora yourself?
MID_EV11_002_m01_019: Course I have. Your old man's got some clout, kid.
MID_EV11_002_m01_020: What a buncha crap. Are you really bragging about—\nHuh? The statue cracked, and there's something...
MID_EV11_002_m01_021: What's this necklace? That's a huge jewel.
MID_EV11_002_m01_022: It's... It's gotta be...
MID_EV11_002_m01_023: Where'd you steal this, Pop?
MID_EV11_002_m01_024: I didn't steal it! That's a keepsake. From your mother.
MID_EV11_002_m01_025: This was...Mom's? Really?
MID_EV11_002_m01_026: I was so little when Mom died. I can't even\nremember her face.
MID_EV11_002_m01_027: Pop...what was Mom like?
MID_EV11_002_m01_028: She was... She was beautiful...and so kind.
MID_EV11_002_m01_029: <NCA>Ask about her beauty.
MID_EV11_002_m01_030: <NCB>Ask about her kindness.
MID_EV11_002_m01_044: <ACA>Was she beautiful like Aurora?
MID_EV11_002_m01_031: <ACA>Heh... Yeah, you could say that.
MID_EV11_002_m01_032: <ACA>Look, she was incredibly beautiful, your mom.\nShe put the moon and stars to shame.
MID_EV11_002_m01_045: <ACB>Kind, like Peter's mom?
MID_EV11_002_m01_033: <ACB>Estie? Nah, it was different.
MID_EV11_002_m01_034: <ACB>Your mom was...soft, gentle, like silk.
MID_EV11_002_m01_035: <ACB>She was so innocent...naïve, maybe. She didn't even\nknow how to use a kitchen knife.
MID_EV11_002_m01_036: <ACB>One time she served up a raw potato, skin and all.\nWe both had upset stomachs for a while after that.
MID_EV11_002_m01_037: Huh. Interesting.
MID_EV11_002_m01_038: Oh! Hey, we had a strange visitor. He said to tell you\n"it's tomorrow."
MID_EV11_002_m01_043: Wait... Quiet.
MID_EV11_003_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_003_m01_001: Those useless dogs failed me. This wreaks havoc on\nmy plans.
MID_EV11_003_m01_002: All that effort to find the Eye... And who is this boy?
MID_EV11_003_m01_003: I've heard that Drake's treasures sometimes choose\ntheir owners.
MID_EV11_003_m01_004: Just as they abandon the unworthy. Perhaps the\ntreasure...chose him?
MID_EV11_003_m01_005: You're wondering if it's taken an interest in the boy?\nWell, Father? Is this true?
MID_EV11_003_m01_006: Who's that? You there!
MID_EV11_003_m01_007: Only one spot with a view of the whole village.\nThought I'd come see who's in charge of this mess.
MID_EV11_003_m01_008: Looks like I'm right on target... Wouldn't you\nsay, beautiful?
MID_EV11_003_m01_009: Stay back!
MID_EV11_003_m01_010: I'm gonna have to ask you to stay put. I've got a few\nquestions, and you're gonna answer 'em.
MID_EV11_003_m01_011: I have a question for you: Do you really think your\nson is safe alone?
MID_EV11_003_m01_012: Don't underestimate that kid. I didn't raise a fool.
MID_EV11_003_m01_014: Who are you anyway? Why're you after\nthat necklace?
MID_EV11_003_m01_015: You must be an imbecile if you think we'll answer\nyour questions.
MID_EV11_003_m01_016: Prepare to die!
MID_EV11_003_m01_017: Madness! My attack is hard as diamond, yet you stop\nit with little effort?
MID_EV11_003_m01_018: I've seen that technique before. It's a vulkan art, no?\nAre you one of them?
MID_EV11_003_m01_019: Wide of the mark but not by much. I can take a\nguess about who you are too.
MID_EV11_003_m01_020: Order of Mithras, right? I tangled with one of yours\na while back.
MID_EV11_003_m01_021: Why'd you come from Dagsion to visit us out here\nin the sticks? Is that necklace really so valuable?
MID_EV11_003_m01_022: I'm taking my leave of this bothersome opponent.
MID_EV11_003_m01_023: You didn't answer my questions yet. Think I'm just\ngonna let you walk?
MID_EV11_003_m01_024: Ahaha.
MID_EV11_003_m01_025: Mm? What...
MID_EV11_003_m01_026: This wind... Is it an illusion?
MID_EV11_003_m01_027: Fine, you win this one. Fooling me with a cheap\ntrick. Real scary, lady.
MID_EV11_003_m01_028: Ack...*cough* *cough*
MID_EV11_003_m01_029: N-not yet... Gotta hold on a little longer...
MID_EV11_004_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_004_m01_001: Hey, not bad out there. You got the necklace, yeah?
MID_EV11_004_m01_002: <NCA>Complain that it wasn't easy.
MID_EV11_004_m01_003: <NCB>Ask what he was doing.
MID_EV11_004_m01_035: <ACA>Yeah, but it was rough! And something\nweird happened.
MID_EV11_004_m01_004: <ACA>I'm sorry I left you to deal with all that.
MID_EV11_004_m01_005: <ACA>But I didn't think a buncha lunkheads would be any\nproblem for you. I was right, wasn't I?
MID_EV11_004_m01_036: <ACB>Yeah. Thanks. And where were you?\nYou disappeared!
MID_EV11_004_m01_006: <ACB>I had a little flash of inspiration, so I took a hike up\nthe hill.
MID_EV11_004_m01_007: <ACB>I found the two puppet masters up there, but they got\naway from me.
MID_EV11_004_m01_008: Pop! Listen to me. The jewel from the necklace got\nstuck in my hand.
MID_EV11_004_m01_009: And then...I don't know what it was, but I got control\nof this power...
MID_EV11_004_m01_010: What? Gimme that hand.
MID_EV11_004_m01_011: What do you think? Any ideas?
MID_EV11_004_m01_012: The way that jewel's set in your hand... I'd swear\nit's in the shape of an eye.
MID_EV11_004_m01_013: I've seen plenty of strange things in my time, but this\nis a first for me.
MID_EV11_004_m01_014: Hmm...
MID_EV11_004_m01_015: Guess there's only one thing to do. And here I\nwas planning on going solo.
MID_EV11_004_m01_016: Pack your bags, Cai. We're headed for Dagsion.
MID_EV11_004_m01_017: What? Kinda sudden, Pop.
MID_EV11_004_m01_018: Dagsion's not a short hike. It takes at least a week\nto get there, right?
MID_EV11_004_m01_019: That necklace came from your mom a long while ago.\nI'm bettin' we'll get answers from...her.
MID_EV11_004_m01_020: Her? What do you mean?
MID_EV11_004_m01_021: Just what I said, "her." What's the matter? Don't you\nwanna meet your mom?
MID_EV11_004_m01_022: But you said Mom died when I was little!
MID_EV11_004_m01_023: Yeah, that wasn't exactly true. I mean, there were\nsome tricky circumstances.
MID_EV11_004_m01_024: You've been lying to me?!
MID_EV11_004_m01_025: You just drop that on me and expect me to take it?!\nYou tricked a helpless little kid!
MID_EV11_004_m01_026: Hey! That's dangerous! Don't swing that around\nin here!
MID_EV11_004_m01_027: Show some respect for Aurora's statue! Hey! Don't\neven think about throwing it! Knock it off!
MID_EV11_004_m01_028: Cai and his dad are going to Dagsion.
MID_EV11_004_m01_029: Oh! I've read all about it. It sounds amazing. I've\nalways dreamed about going to the city.
MID_EV11_004_m01_030: There was something about meeting Cai's mom too.
MID_EV11_004_m01_031: No way! I definitely want to get to know her.
MID_EV11_004_m01_032: We can't just hang around here. Let's get ready to go!
MID_EV11_004_m01_033: I don't get it. Are they gonna visit her grave?
MID_EV11_004_m01_034: Don't worry about it. Let's ambush them as they're\nleaving the village, and we'll go with them. Hurry up!